<title>BARBADOS: CRICKET-RED STRIPE CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RED STRIPE CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>BRIDGETOWN 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the final day of</p>
<p>four-day Red Stripe Cup cricket matches on Monday:</p>
<p>In Kingston: Trinidad and Tobago beat Jamaica by 45 runs.</p>
<p>Trinidad and Tobago 160 and 245 (D.Williams 56; F.Rose 4-89).</p>
<p>Jamaica 226 and 134 (R.Samuels 55).</p>
<p>In Charlestown, Nevis: Leeward Islands drew with Guyana.</p>
<p>Guyana 257 and 264 (Z.Haniff 71, A.Haniff 62; W.Phillip 5-108).</p>
<p>Leeward Islands 221 (K.Arthurton 61, R.Powell 51; M.Nagamootoo</p>
<p>4-88) and 129-1 (A.Adams 69 not out, Arthurton 45 not out).</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, lost, drawn, no</p>
<p>result, points)</p>
<p> Barbados		  9   6   1   2   0   112</p>
<p> Jamaica		   9   3   2   3   1    77</p>
<p> Trinidad and Tobago   9   3   1   4   1    76</p>
<p> Leeward Islands	 9   3   2   2   2    64</p>
<p> Guyana		    9   0   1   5   3    40</p>
<p> Windward Islands	9   0   8   0   1    19</p>
<p>(Note: Windwards earned 15 points for three games which they</p>
<p>led on first innings but were beaten).</p>
</text>
